-- A DISCORD BOT, WRITTEN IN POLITELANG
--
-- A bot is a loop. It listens, looks at what was said, and answers. That is the whole shape of it,
-- and writing it that way means there are no handlers, no callbacks and nothing to register --
-- only a program that reads from the top downwards.
--
-- This does not run in the reference runner, which has no network and does not want one. Write it
-- out as JavaScript and run it with node:
--
--     polite build examples/discord/hello-bot.polite
--     cd examples/discord
--     npm install discord.js
--     node hello-bot.mjs
--
-- The token is never written in here. It is read from the surroundings the program was started in,
-- so this file can be shown to anybody without handing them the keys to the bot.
--
-- Written in PoliteLang by Creeperdiamonds Studios.


-- The greetings worth answering. Kept in one place, so that adding one is adding a line.
please define a greeting with a said:
    remember greetings is an empty list
    add "hello" to greetings
    add "hi" to greetings
    add "hey" to greetings
    add "good morning" to greetings
    add "good evening" to greetings
    give back greetings contains said
thank you for defining


please define the help:
    remember lines is an empty list
    add "Here is everything I know how to do:" to lines
    add "" to lines
    add "  hello           I will say hello back" to lines
    add "  !ping           I will say pong" to lines
    add "  !where          I will say which channel and server we are in" to lines
    add "  !say <words>    I will say those words" to lines
    add "  !count <words>  I will count the words" to lines
    add "  !help           this" to lines
    add "  !goodbye        I will stop" to lines
    give back the join of lines with "\n"
thank you for defining


please show ""
please show "  A POLITE BOT"
please show ""

-- Starting is the one part that has to work. If it does not, there is no bot to run.
please try to:
    log in to discord with the secret called "DISCORD_TOKEN"
    let my status be "listening politely"
otherwise if it does not work out:
    show "  I could not start, because {what went wrong}"
    show ""
    stop everything
thank you for trying

please show "  Waiting to be spoken to. Press control and C to stop."
please show ""

please remember answered is 0
please remember going is yes

please keep going forever:
    check if not going:
        stop repeating
    thanks

    -- Everything to do with one message sits inside here, so that a message the bot cannot
    -- answer -- because it was not allowed to speak, or because the connection hiccuped -- costs
    -- that one message and not the whole evening.
    try to:
        listen for the next message

        remember spoken is what they said
        remember said is the small letters of the trimmed version of spoken
        show "  {their name} in {the channel it came from}: {spoken}"

        check if they are a bot:
            show "    (a bot, so I left it alone)"
        otherwise if a greeting with said:
            reply with "Hello, {their name}. I hope your day is going well."
            change answered to answered plus 1
        otherwise if said is "!ping":
            reply with "Pong."
            change answered to answered plus 1
        otherwise if said is "!help":
            reply with the help
            change answered to answered plus 1
        otherwise if said is "!where":
            reply with "We are in {the channel it came from}, on {the server it came from}."
            change answered to answered plus 1
        otherwise if said starts with "!say ":
            send the piece of spoken from 6 to (the length of spoken)
            change answered to answered plus 1
        otherwise if said starts with "!count ":
            remember rest is the piece of spoken from 8 to (the length of spoken)
            remember many is the number of items in the words in rest
            reply with "That is {many} words."
            change answered to answered plus 1
        otherwise if said is "!goodbye":
            reply with "Goodbye. Thank you for having me."
            change going to no
        thank you for checking
    otherwise if it does not work out:
        show "    (that one did not work out: {what went wrong})"
    thank you for trying
thank you for repeating

please show ""
please show "  The bot has stopped, after answering {answered} times."
please show ""
